--- body ---
## Context

`prompt_version` (in `method_params`) identifies which prompt was used.
Convention: `prompt_{version}.txt` for static prompts (findable by
inspection); `prompt_{version}.py` for programmatic prompts (DSPy).
This ticket renames existing files to match and defines the full vocabulary.

## prompt_version vocabulary

| prompt_version | File                   | What it asks for                      |
|----------------|------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| extract        | prompt_extract.txt     | Terse CSV extraction (one-liner)      |
| complete       | prompt_complete.txt    | Full sourced inventory + bibliography |
| scenarios      | prompt_scenarios.txt   | 3-scenario modelling study to 2050    |
| cited          | prompt_cited.txt       | Terse extraction + citation columns   |
| followups      | prompt_followups.txt   | Conversational follow-up questions    |
| per_fuel       | (assembled at runtime) | Per-fuel subprompts via query runner  |
| base           | (modules/ assembled)   | No modules — ablation zero point      |
| composite      | (modules/ assembled)   | All 6 modules — ablation ceiling      |
| +persona       | (modules/ assembled)   | base + persona module                 |
| -persona       | (modules/ assembled)   | composite − persona module            |
| … (±aspect)    | (modules/ assembled)   | One per module, both arms             |
| dspy           | prompt_dspy.txt        | DSPy/MIPROv2 compiled output          |

## File renames

- `prompt_structured.txt`         → `prompt_extract.txt`
- `prompt_frontier.txt`           → `prompt_complete.txt`
- `prompt_frontier_scenarios.txt` → `prompt_scenarios.txt`
- `prompt_structured_sourced.txt` → `prompt_cited.txt`
- `followups.txt`                 → `prompt_followups.txt`
- `prompt_frontier_skill.txt`     → DELETE (ticket 0120 purge)

## Actions

1. Rename the five prompt files above; update all references in
   `experiments.toml`, `harness.py`, and any script that loads
   prompts by path.
2. Delete `prompt_frontier_skill.txt`.
3. Audit `modules/` names for self-descriptiveness. `base.txt` is the
   always-included foundation — confirm its role is documented in
   `prompts/README.md`; rename only if unclear to a fresh reader.
4. Coordinate with 0120: harness emits ablation `prompt_version` as the
   sign-notation label derived from sweep name or active module list;
   migration script back-fills existing records (currently `"derived"`).
5. Run `make test` green.

## Exit criteria

- No file named `prompt_structured*.txt`, `prompt_frontier*.txt`,
  or bare `followups.txt` remains in `experiments/prompts/`.
- Each static `prompt_version` maps to `prompt_{version}.txt`.
- Ablation labels documented in `prompts/README.md`.
- `make test` green.
- Unblocks 0120.


